full_text:
A District Court decision overturning major provisions of three Executive Orders has been appealed. Here is a summary of the 30-page Memorandum Opinion.
The decision, written by Judge Leon, held that President Trump's EO-13 (January 25, 2017), EO-25 (March 6, 2017), and EO-13 (February 24, 2017) are unlawful in part because they:
1. Overstepped the President's statutory authority under the INA (Immigration and Nationality Act) to restrict entry into the US;
2. Discriminated against individuals based on their religion, which violates the First Amendment's Establishment Clause;
3. Violated the Equal Protection Clause of the Fifth Amendment by favoring certain religions

